WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:03.068
Narrator: Last, what this first pass can't tell me.

2
00:00:03.068 --> 00:00:06.139
Narrator: A screen reader shows whether things work as built,

3
00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.849
Narrator: not whether they help the people they're for.

4
00:00:08.849 --> 00:00:13.125
Narrator: These need people with disabilities, on their own devices and settings.

5
00:00:13.778 --> 00:00:15.863
Keyboard: Tab → link, Skip to content

6
00:00:15.863 --> 00:00:17.864
Keyboard: Tab → button, Describe this page

7
00:00:17.864 --> 00:00:19.665
Keyboard: Return → heading, The home page

8
00:00:19.665 --> 00:00:21.420
Narrator: First, Describe this page.

9
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.215
Narrator: Does a written description of the layout help someone picture the page?

10
00:00:26.215 --> 00:00:28.174
Narrator: Is it too long, or too short?

11
00:00:28.174 --> 00:00:32.361
Narrator: Blind people who use a screen reader every day should tell us,

12
00:00:32.361 --> 00:00:34.589
Narrator: on VoiceOver and on JAWS or NVDA.

13
00:00:35.221 --> 00:00:37.084
Keyboard: Escape → button, Describe this page

14
00:00:37.084 --> 00:00:40.142
Narrator: Second, other screen readers and devices.

15
00:00:40.142 --> 00:00:43.124
Narrator: This pass used VoiceOver in Safari only,

16
00:00:43.124 --> 00:00:49.089
Narrator: and its biggest finding came from how Safari passes hidden content to VoiceOver.

17
00:00:49.089 --> 00:00:54.160
Narrator: JAWS, NVDA, VoiceOver on iPhone and TalkBack all behave differently.

18
00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.422
Keyboard: Tab → link, Marcelo Paiva

19
00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:58.044
Keyboard: Tab → link, Writing

20
00:00:58.044 --> 00:00:59.711
Keyboard: Tab → link, Work

21
00:00:59.711 --> 00:01:01.464
Keyboard: Tab → link, Signal

22
00:01:01.464 --> 00:01:03.084
Keyboard: Tab → link, Tools

23
00:01:03.084 --> 00:01:04.742
Keyboard: Tab → link, Resume

24
00:01:04.742 --> 00:01:06.398
Keyboard: Tab → button, Set for you, collapsed

25
00:01:06.398 --> 00:01:08.219
Keyboard: Return → button, Set for you, expanded

26
00:01:08.219 --> 00:01:11.373
Narrator: Third, Set for you reads its settings as a sentence.

27
00:01:11.373 --> 00:01:15.801
Narrator: Whether that feels natural, and whether the new announcements are enough,

28
00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:20.594
Narrator: is for screen reader users, and people with cognitive or learning disabilities,

29
00:01:20.594 --> 00:01:21.019
Narrator: to say.

30
00:01:21.643 --> 00:01:23.520
Keyboard: Escape → button, Set for you, collapsed

31
00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:29.041
Narrator: Fourth, motion. The drawings drift and the background moves. The pause button works…

32
00:01:29.041 --> 00:01:33.511
Narrator: but is it found in time, and is the motion comfortable before it is?

33
00:01:33.511 --> 00:01:36.470
Narrator: People with vestibular disorders can tell us.

34
00:01:37.095 --> 00:01:39.314
Keyboard: Command-Plus: zooms the page

35
00:01:39.314 --> 00:01:41.504
Keyboard: Command-Plus: zooms the page

36
00:01:41.504 --> 00:01:43.479
Keyboard: Command-Plus: zooms the page

37
00:01:43.479 --> 00:01:45.549
Narrator: Fifth, zoom and magnification.

38
00:01:45.549 --> 00:01:50.934
Narrator: Zoomed in, the header stays at the top, and some text sits over moving colour.

39
00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:55.904
Narrator: People with low vision who use zoom or a screen magnifier should try it.

40
00:01:56.521 --> 00:01:58.516
Keyboard: Command-0: back to actual size

41
00:01:58.516 --> 00:02:00.912
Narrator: Sixth, voice control and switch access.

42
00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:05.827
Narrator: Names were checked for what a screen reader says, not for what people say aloud,

43
00:02:05.827 --> 00:02:10.866
Narrator: and the home page has more than fifty stops for someone moving one step at a time.

44
00:02:11.494 --> 00:02:13.541
Keyboard: Return → button, Set for you, expanded

45
00:02:13.541 --> 00:02:15.184
Keyboard: Tab → pop-up button, Drawings, in calm color

46
00:02:15.184 --> 00:02:16.770
Keyboard: Tab → pop-up button, Theme, following my device

47
00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:18.331
Keyboard: Tab → pop-up button, Motion, allowed

48
00:02:18.331 --> 00:02:19.910
Keyboard: Tab → pop-up button, Home page, a list of essays

49
00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.410
Keyboard: Focus is on → pop-up button, Home page, a list of essays

50
00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:22.839
Keyboard: Escape → button, Set for you, collapsed

51
00:02:22.839 --> 00:02:28.263
Narrator: And last, the collage. Set for you can turn the home page into a field of drawings.

52
00:02:28.263 --> 00:02:30.289
Narrator: This pass tested the list only.

53
00:02:30.841 --> 00:02:33.069
Narrator: That's the end of the first pass.

54
00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:37.999
Narrator: Five problems found on the page: three fixed and live, one fix in review,

55
00:02:37.999 --> 00:02:39.282
Narrator: and one still open.

56
00:02:39.282 --> 00:02:41.241
Narrator: The next test is with people.
